# 24. RISK ASSESSMENT

A simplified model:

> **Risk ≈ Likelihood × Impact**

Example:

```text
Critical database
+
Internet exposure
+
Weak authentication
        ↓
High risk
```

Risk is not determined by vulnerability severity alone.

---

# 25. SECURITY CONTROL MATURITY

A simple maturity model:

| Level | Description |
|---|---|
| 1 | Ad hoc |
| 2 | Developing |
| 3 | Defined |
| 4 | Managed |
| 5 | Optimized |

Example:

### Level 1

No formal patch process.

### Level 3

Defined patch policy and schedule.

### Level 5

Automated, continuously measured and improved patch management.

---

# 26. POSTURE SCORECARD

Example:

| Area | Score |
|---|---:|
| Asset Management | 4/5 |
| Identity Security | 3/5 |
| Network Security | 4/5 |
| Endpoint Security | 4/5 |
| Application Security | 3/5 |
| Logging | 2/5 |
| Backup | 4/5 |
